  "generated_text": "To round \\(\\frac{4}{7}\\) to the nearest tenth, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Convert the fraction to a decimal:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{4}{7} \\approx 0.5714285714285714\n   \\]\n\n2. **Identify the tenths and hundredths place:**\n   - The tenths place is the first digit to the right of the decimal point.\n   - The hundredths place is the second digit to the right of the decimal point.\n   From our decimal, \\(0.5714285714285714\\), the tenths place is \\(5\\) and the hundredths place is \\(7\\).\n\n3. **Determine if the hundredths place digit is 5 or greater:**\n   - The hundredths place digit is \\(7\\), which is greater than \\(5\\).\n\n4. **Apply the rounding rule:**\n   - If the digit in the hundredths place is \\(5\\) or greater, we round up the digit in the tenths place.\n   - Here, the tenths place digit \\(5\\) will be rounded up to \\(6\\).\n\n5. **Form the rounded decimal:**\n   - The rounded number to the nearest tenth is \\(0.6\\).\n\nTherefore, \\(\\frac{4}{7}\\) rounded to the nearest tenth is \\(\\boxed{0.6}\\).",
